; Vendored Fmt (see README.md). The sources are byte-identical to upstream, so
; the enclosing asm/dune marks this tree `vendored_dirs`: dune then suppresses
; warnings here and leaves it out of `@fmt`, which keeps the copy verifiable
; against its recorded hashes.
;
; The vendored copy is what makes Fmt usable here at all: the opam `fmt` package
; is built by topkg and installs a META template, which dune rejects for Melange
; ("not compatible with melange support"), so the production closure could not
; depend on it and still satisfy .ai/asm_plan.md §11.6.
;
; Melange mode lives in melange/vendor/fmt, which copy_files these same sources.
(library
 (name fmt)
 (modes byte native)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))
